<!-- -*- xml -*- -->
<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      type="topic"
      id="camera-focusing">
  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#main"/>

    <desc>Controlling camera focus during image preview</desc>
  </info>
  <title>Camera Focus</title>

  <p>
    As mentioned in the <link xref="image-preview"/> section, no
    attempt is made to activate the autofocus mechanism when capturing
    from preview mode, instead the user has full control over
    focusing via number of keyboard shortcuts.
  </p>

  <p>
    To trigger autofocus at any time press the <key>a</key>, or use
    the autofocus button in the toolbar while live preview is active.
    If the camera is unable to achieve focus, for example, due to
    low lighting conditions or a subject that is too close to
    the lens, an error may be displayed.
  </p>

  <p>
    While live preview is active, clicking on the preview image moves
    the camera focus point to that position and triggers autofocus.
    This requires the camera to support a movable focus point. When
    necessary, <app>Entangle</app> switches the camera into a Flexible
    Spot focus area mode automatically. The red focus point overlay
    shows the selected position; it can be disabled in the Image Viewer
    preferences.
  </p>

  <p>
    A vertical slider on the right edge of the preview moves the lens
    focus in manual focus mode. The slider returns to the centre after
    each step and is only enabled while live preview is active and the
    camera supports manual focus adjustment.
  </p>

  <p>
    To manually focus, the lens can be moved in either direction
    at two levels of granularity. Small shifts in focal point
    can be made using the <key>,</key> and <key>.</key> keys.
    Moderate shifts in focal point can be made using the
    <key>&lt;</key> and <key>&gt;</key> keys. If the limit of
    focusing is reached in either direction, an error may be
    displayed.
  </p>

  <note style="important">
    <p>
      To control focusing from <app>Entangle</app>, the camera body
      <em>and</em> lens <em>must</em> both have their respective
      autofocus switches activated. If either are set to manual
      focus, <app>Entangle</app> will be unable to perform autofocus
      or manual focusing.
    </p>
  </note>
</page>
